{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.54,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Emit the `second-started` marker only after the contender has actually attempted/reached the blocking lock (or add a signal proving the flock call was entered) so the 0.2s absence assertion cannot pass merely because the child is slow to reach lock acquisition.","criteria":["tests"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py:43-44: `events.send(\"second-started\")` is emitted, then `marker.remove_marker(ticket_dir)` is called — the started signal precedes the lock attempt","tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py:110-111: `assert event_rx.recv() == \"second-started\"` then `assert not event_rx.poll(timeout=0.2)`","src/rebar/reducer/marker.py:74-79: remove_marker's blocking flock is inside `_marker_lock`; the test has no signal proving the contender reached that acquisition before the 0.2s poll expired"],"finding":"The core serialization proof `assert not event_rx.poll(timeout=0.2)` (line 111) does not establish that the second process actually reached the lock-acquisition point before the window elapsed. The contender sends `second-started` BEFORE calling `remove_marker`, so the absence of a `second-done` message within 0.2s is equally consistent with 'blocked on the cross-process flock' (the behavior under test) and 'the spawned child has not yet reached the take_blocking_exclusive call'. A regression that broke cross-process serialization would not be reliably caught if child startup/scheduling delayed the flock call past the 0.2s window.","id":"0","impact":0.0,"location":"tests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py:111","norm_id":"nfc83f22f537ae459","priority":0.0,"reason":